Description: token broker for AI agents - the door a component answers at
 serve is how every component is reached and the only way anything leaves one.
 It takes the ask as an argument or from standard input, holds it to the
 contract the component says it takes, runs the component with nothing but the
 document, holds what comes back to the contract the component says it gives,
 and writes that to standard output or to a file closed to everyone but its
 owner. Nothing is written until the answer has been admitted.
 .
 It carries no contract of its own, for the same reason parse and format do
 not. What a component says it speaks is the contract packages it depends on.
 .
 A component behind a door reads one document and writes one, and is told
 nothing about how it was reached. What carries the document can therefore be
 replaced - a socket, a listener on the privileged side of a boundary - without
 the component being touched.

